# The Last Green World - a world plan of the library (SL11): Verdance, the last land where things still grow
# A main story in place of Raft's (Raft's own story off, random islands off: Verdance should feel like one land): ten
# islands from a pollen-dusted spit to the Heart of Green and the Rootcore under it, following the Seedkeepers who grew a
# living organism to green the drowned world - and lost control of it. Ranger Oda Fenn's logs lead the way; the goat
# Burr finds what she hid. At the Heart the player turns one valve, BURN or SPREAD, and the Rootcore is finished the same
# way. Thornback Ridge, a hermit's camp, turns up ahead on day 6. Raft's story blueprints are quest steps on the way.
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe plan_last_green_world) in the editor's World plans window. Its play test:
# content\tests\plan_last_green_world.play.
plan new The Last Green World
plan description Verdance, the last land where things still grow: a pollen spit, a ranger station, a river delta, a tracker's hill, a grove of giant trees, root caves, a poisoned marsh, a stair of roots, and the Heart of Green with the Rootcore beneath it - where one valve decides what Verdance becomes Its quest islands are as big as Raft's own big islands.
plan random off
plan story off
plan rule spit | island:Pollenreach Spit | start | receiver:500 | The Receiver hisses, then a calm recorded voice: "Verdance Ranger Service. Landing beacon on Pollenreach Spit." | Pollenreach Spit | first | quest
plan rule landing | island:Ranger Landing | quest:spit | receiver:700 | The spit's beacon hands over to the ranger station's band, 700: a hen clucking near the microphone. | Ranger Landing | after:spit | quest
plan rule delta | island:Riverfork Delta | visit:landing | receiver:800 | From the station mast the Receiver finds a river outpost on 800, its relay ticking. | Riverfork Delta | after:landing | quest
plan rule rise | island:Tracker's Rise | step:delta:6 | receiver:700 | Upriver, a ranger's tower calls on 700: "Tracker's Rise. The herds are back on the meadow." | Tracker's Rise | after:delta | step:8
plan rule grove | island:Hollowtrunk Grove | quest:rise | receiver:900 | On 900, wind in very tall trees and a watering rota read aloud: Hollowtrunk Grove. | Hollowtrunk Grove | after:rise | zone:roots
plan rule caves | island:Rootweave Caves | zone:grove:roots | receiver:600 | Down among the roots the Receiver picks up a survey team's beacon on 600, from under a hill. | Rootweave Caves | after:grove | quest
plan rule mire | island:Blightmire | quest:caves | receiver:1000:needs=engine | On 1000, far off and faint, a smelter camp's call: "Blightmire. Bring fire." | Blightmire | after:caves | signal:cleansed
plan rule canopy | island:Canopy Stair | rule:mire | receiver:900 | With the marsh clean, the Seedkeepers' last camp answers on 900: a stair of roots, north. | Canopy Stair | after:mire | quest
plan rule heart | island:The Heart of Green | quest:canopy | receiver:1200 | On 1200, a slow hum like a heartbeat - the Heart of Green, at the centre of Verdance. | The Heart of Green | after:canopy | step:23
plan rule rootcore | island:The Rootcore | signal:heart:below | receiver:400 | Under the Heart, on 400, warm static: the Rootcore, breathing. | The Rootcore | after:heart | quest
plan rule ridge | island:Thornback Ridge | day:6 | ahead:500 | Ahead, a thorny ridge with a thin line of smoke from a ledge halfway up. | Thornback Ridge
plan credits The Last Green World | Custom Islands
plan ending One seed from the oldest root, warm in your hand. Whatever Verdance becomes now, it began again with you.\n\nThe end of The Last Green World.
plan save
